# rule.prefer.decompose-a-subject-via-suffixes

when a subject grows a distinct sub-claim, eject it into a suffixed peer. do not accrete it inline.

```
$subject._.md            # root — the whole, plus an index of zoom-ins
$subject.$zoom.md        # one zoom-in per sub-claim, a peer of the root
```

the root carries a pointer, never the zoom's body. (`rule.require.summary-at-the-cluster-root` names the root; this says whether to split.)

| when… | then… |
|---|---|
| you would add a `##` section for a claim that stands alone | eject, leave a pointer |
| a section has its own subsections, examples, enforcement | it is a brief; give it a file |
| a reader wants it once, not every boot | dereference case |
| a section explains why where the root states what | the why is the zoom |
| you reach for a new top-level name for a sub-claim | a suffix declares the parent; a peer name hides it |
| a subject has one claim | leave it; fires on the split only |

## .the suffix names the zoom, not an ordinal

```
👎  philosophy.entoolment-is-the-pinnacle.2.md
👍  philosophy.entoolment-is-the-pinnacle.via-routes.md
```

## .a zoom is not a fork

pointer owed both ways: root names zoom by path and when to reach for it; zoom names its root. the zoom holds one facet in depth and never restates the root.

blocker: sub-claim under a new top-level name · zoom with no pointer from root or no back-pointer · zoom that restates its root · suffix that is an ordinal or non-name.
nitpick: self-contained sub-claim accreted inline.
false positive: single-claim brief left whole.

⇒ `rule.require.summary-at-the-cluster-root` · `rule.require.rules-are-clusters`
